WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
<b>Film</b>

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:04.210
We've definitely got to add all 
the coloring and sound effects

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:05.230
we had to skip last time.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:07.200
Definitely. We definitely do!

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.440
A story, too! I want it to be 
even better than last time!

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.360
Even better!

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:18.280
<b>96 days until the culture festival

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.330
If we're going to have dialog, 
that means we need voice actors, right?

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.820
We'll need to hold auditions.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.280
I'd wait until the storyboard 
is done to worry about that.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.390
What about backgrounds?

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:21.370
Colored this time. Naturally, I'll—

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:25.250
The art club actually wants 
to help us out this time.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.660
They said our work

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:30.330
made an impression on them at the 
budget committee, much like the robot club.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.040
Huh, that's pretty cool.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.660
I'm sure they realize they 
can get something out of it.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.490
As soon as Asakusa finishes the storyboards,

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.470
we'll meet with them to 
hash out the backgrounds.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:40.330
A meeting...

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:44.470
You're going to need to explain 
to them what kind of art we need.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:47.440
I-I can't tell people what to do...

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:51.410
Well, you also can't draw the backgrounds 
for every cut on your own, can you?

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.110
No groaning, moaning, or excuses.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:56.830
There's one other hurdle to deal with.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:01.950
The robot club has requested that an 
opening sequence be included.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:05.190
Greatest, Strongest
Robot Song

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.160
The song is already in the works, apparently.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:12.420
<b>Lots of Nutrition!
Allgrapes
Natural Sweetness</b>

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:12.420
<b>Bright Day
Milk</b>

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:12.420
<b>Bright Day
Milk</b>

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:12.420
<b>Egg Biscuits</b>

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:12.420
<b>A</b>

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:12.420
<b>Cola</b>

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:12.420
<b>Recommended for
 7 months and up</b>

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:08.780
We'll discuss it in more detail 
once the demo track is ready.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.990
What about the music during the actual film?

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:12.420
I think it should be epic!

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:17.310
Could you handle that, Mizusaki?

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:20.670
Never done it before. 
What about you, Asakusa?

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.790
I've never had a chance to try before.

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:28.650
I'll ask around to see if 
anyone I know writes music.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:32.080
We've got three times the amount 
of time for production...

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.820
But will our club activity 
time be enough, Mizusaki?

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.400
No way! I've gotta work at home, too!

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:41.160
Animating designs with so many 
lines is a ton of work, y'know.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:45.450
They say you're not a real animator 
until you can do 500 pieces of art a month,

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:48.170
but for anime, you need to be able 
to draw the necessary amount of art

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.020
at the required standard of quality,

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:54.760
which is nothing like randomly dashing 
off 500 doodles of whatever you want!

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:57.380
How difficult is it, exactly?

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:03.500
Imagine having to draw 500 rough drafts 
while wearing gloves and handcuffs,

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:07.060
and if you're even 0.02 millimeters 
off from frame to frame, you end up in hell.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.940
But even before that, imagine having 
to uniformly draw ten pieces of art

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.070
that accurately move a millimeter at a time, 
while wearing armor, or you starve.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.260
Having to draw three pieces 
of art, every hour,

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.010
with so many lines, while thinking
 about how it moves?

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:18.780
It's basically a curse!

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.130
Producing anime while in 
high school is impossible!

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:25.490
So the entire premise of this club is invalid.

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:30.300
How are things coming along
 for you, Asakusa?

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.580
So far, so good!

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.660
I'm pretty sure that can't be the case 
since we're having to adjust the schedule

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.660
based on your progress with the storyboards.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.800
Mizusaki, do you have any suggestions 
for how we can improve our efficiency?

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:44.010
Well, it'd definitely be faster if 
we had a computer in the club room.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.090
That way, we can handle the finishing 
touches and the photography here.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:49.850
Having to use the PC room every time 
we need to make slight adjustments

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:51.950
definitely eats up time.

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:54.780
I'm heading out.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:02.030
<b><i>Episode 6        Let's Do Better Than Last Time!</i></b>

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.400
<b><i>Keep</i></b>

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:58.770
<b><i>Your</i></b>

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.320
<b><i>Hands</i></b>

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:03.700
<b><i>Off</i></b>

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:14.690
<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:22.900
<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.620
Kanamori never came back, huh?

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:32.990
I imagine she went home.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.310
Main
Gate

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.420
Let's get something to eat.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:43.100
Kanamori is inviting us out to eat?

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:46.540
Wh-What is this place?

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.180
Does it look like a shoe store?

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.770
<b>R
a
m
e
n</b>

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:50.960
I can smell gasoline. Is this a good idea?

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.770
A few fumes never killed anybody.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.270
This is my treat.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:56.860
Whuzzat?!

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:57.560
Really?

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.550
Whoa, hold on! This is 
Kanamori we're talking about!

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:01.780
Nothing is scarier than a 
free meal from the yakuza!

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:03.180
It's fine.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:04.460
I've just got ulterior motives.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:05.990
That's the scary part!

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:09.380
Think of it as an advance 
on your overtime.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.200
Since we're going to have 
to work on this project

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.300
outside of club hours to finish it.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:17.750
<b>Pickled</b>

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:17.750
<b>Garlic</b>

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.130
That's more considerate than I would've figured.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.750
Hardly. I'm only doing the obvious thing.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.460
You'll be expected to work it off, eventually.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:29.220
<b>Bamboo Shoots</b>

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:29.220
<b>Seaweed & Salt</b>

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:29.220
<b>Roasted Pork</b>

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:29.220
<b>Ramen</b>

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:25.050
Kake ramen!

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:25.850
Red pepper, please.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.730
Can I get a soft-boiled egg in mine? 
With extra wakame!

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:28.650
And firm noodles?

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:29.530
Sure thing!

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:32.670
So, Asakusa, have you made any 
progress with the storyboards?

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:34.220
Es perfecto!

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.290
The time is before school is open.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:38.930
That'll save us the trouble 
of drawing people.

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:40.330
Good idea.

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:43.500
Generally speaking, it's the 
same layout as Shibahama High.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.090
<b>Brrrmm... 
Brrrmm...</b>

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:46.810
There are eerie movements underground.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:49.240
<b>Whoosh...</b>

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:49.240
<b>The water shoots up!</b>

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.240
<b>Splash</b>

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.240
There's a sudden spray of water!

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.990
Here we have the base.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:55.830
Computer Room

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:55.910
Observation Tower

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.710
The first and second floor 
are directly connected!

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:55.790
Looks good.

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:59.670
For various reasons, the robot
 is now eight meters tall.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.350
That's a fair bit bigger.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:03.710
We'll need to confer with the robot club.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:14.170
They're alerted to the monster's appearance!

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.640
There have been reports about 
vibrations being detected underground.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.640
<b>Darker than the last cut
\h\h\h\h\h\h(but power is still on)
\h\h\h\h\h\h Monitor is lit brightly</b>

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.920
<b>Wall</b>

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.920
<b>Rotating emergency light</b>

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:25.150
<b>Voice on the Radio:
"It's a monster.
 A crab-type monster
 has appeared!"</b>

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.150
<b>Captain:
"Move out!
 Everyone, to your positions!"</b>

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:34.660
<b>A1 (In Shadow) 
 A2 (Normal)</b>

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:31.890
The robot is being mobilized!

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.530
The team rushes to their positions!

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:41.090
Off go the bolts!

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:43.130
<b>Underwater</b>

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:44.100
The gate opens!

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.920
<b>Bottom of Gate</b>

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.550
<b>Outer Wall (Bright)</b>

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:50.800
Light up the rails!

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:55.560
All the various machines come 
alive in a dizzying fashion!

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:57.560
<b>Preparing Launch</b>

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:58.600
<b>Launching</b>

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:58.600
It launches!

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.140
Ejected from the catapult!

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:02.990
It encounters the crabtle underground
 before the creature escapes,

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:05.620
but once it re-appears on the 
school grounds, they battle!

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:06.820
The robot wins! The end!

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.100
Here you go.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.700
The others will be a bit longer.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.220
Go ahead and eat.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:12.200
Appreciate it.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.590
<b>SHIBA8 is lit up 

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:14.140
Time to eat!

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:18.210
These action scenes are extremely... 
broad, to put it lightly.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:19.960
That's all up here.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.100
Well, it needs to be on the damn page!

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.370
How is this "perfecto"?! 
You're supposed to be specific!

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:27.360
I'm not good at action, okay?!

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:30.090
I've been drawing a bit of action myself.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:34.670
The arm shakes from the impact of the blow!

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:36.940
It pulls a leg back to avoid 
from getting too close.

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:38.120
That's cool!

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:42.140
And then, the arm is knocked back 
from the recoil of an attack!

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:44.290
The movements leading into a charge...

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:47.570
The wind-up for a punch...

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:49.820
When you're trying to show a powerful hit,

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.890
you need to include these little movements!

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.210
That's some high-quality acting.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:58.080
Why don't we let Mizusaki 
choreograph the action scenes?

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.170
No objections.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:01.410
Here's your kake ramen.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.460
Sorry, the red pepper ramen's 
gonna take a little bit longer.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.240
Time to eat!

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:08.940
I wanted to ask, what're we 
gonna do about sound effects?

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:10.690
They're really important.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.270
Good question. What should we do?

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:19.120
For now, I can look into 
using royalty-free ones.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:22.140
That reminds me, I've made 
arrangements for a computer.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.210
How much was it?

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:25.060
Thirty-two thousand yen.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.810
That is a thuggishly low price!

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:30.240
I talked to the information 
service research group.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:33.420
Apparently, every time they 
put together a new PC,

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:37.170
they dispose of the old one, 
no matter how powerful it was.

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:38.340
Like when they tear down new buildings

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:40.040
just to throw up newer ones.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.620
What about the software and other stuff?

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.030
It's already taken care of.

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:44.510
It is?!

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:47.290
You sure about this, Kanamori?

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:49.930
We're not gonna get raided later, are we?

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:53.250
Would you put a sock in it already,
 you cowardly raccoon dog?

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:58.830
For the software... the school 
already had paid for the licenses.

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:01.970
So it's... basically free.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.630
Here you are. One red pepper ramen.

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.650
I guess this is part of why she's so tall.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.190
Her ramen's gonna get cold.

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:15.900
Okay, I'm ready to start 
drawing when I get home!

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:19.320
If we're doing this on PC, there's a
 tablet at home I can animate on.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:20.860
You sure you won't get caught?

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:23.200
It's easy to hide stuff when you're in bed!

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.900
I'm gonna be animating at home and on the train!

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:28.880
Our goal this time is to complete this anime!

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:33.150
Completion isn't our goal, 
it's a predetermined outcome!

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:39.530
We're not starting production, 
we've already started!

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.260
That is a terrifying way to eat.

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:44.560
Thank you for the food! Check, please!

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:47.720
That'll be 2,450 yen!

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.350
Separate tickets, please.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:52.270
I make it a point to never 
carry more than 1,000 yen.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:54.620
I'll pay you back for the ramen later.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:55.690
What the heck?!

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:59.740
<b>Student Council</b>

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:59.740
The robot club explained what's up.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:02.200
The student council has to 
track the flow of money.

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:04.930
Why, are you going to tax us?

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:08.320
It's just a simple check to make 
sure it's not being misused.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:12.970
We've got a lot of crazy clubs, 
like yours, and it keeps us busy.

